  class LimitedPurposesValueListEntryValuesEnum(_messages.Enum):
    r"""LimitedPurposesValueListEntryValuesEnum enum type.

    Values:
      PROCESSING_PURPOSE_UNSPECIFIED: The processing purpose is unset
      PROCESSING_PURPOSE_NOTHING: <no description>
      PROVISION_OF_SERVICE: Data is being processed as part of normal
        provision of service. Provision of service is in general anything done
        with user consent, that is visible for the user or impacts the user.
        DO NOT USE this value for any processing that is used to provide
        advertising or other revenue generating features specifically related
        to advertising
      PROVISION_OF_SERVICE_INFRASTRUCTURE: Data is being accessed as part of
        normal provision of a multi-tenant infrastructure (e.g., a storage
        system).
      ADS_RELATED_PROVISION_OF_SERVICE: Data is being processed to provide
        advertising or other revenue generation features specifically related
        to advertising
      PRODUCT_PERSONALIZATION: Data is being processed to provide
        personalization features.
      CONTEXTUALIZATION: Data is being processed to provide contextualization
        features, excluding ad-related contextualization.
      REVENUE_GENERATION: Data is being processed to drive revenue that is not
        related to ads (service related revenue).
      USER_SUPPORT: This category is for any data access that was caused by,
        pursuant to, or necessary to resolve an interaction with a customer or
        user that the customer initiated.
      CLOUD_PROCESSING_INFRASTRUCTURE: This processing purpose is configured
        automatically for applicable requests flowing through GCP
        infrastructure. Data is processed through Cloud infrastructure that
        exclusively acts on user instruction. This infrastructure only serves
        Business Users.
      CLOUD_PROCESSING_INFRASTRUCTURE_VALIDATION: This processing purpose is
        programmatically configured for requests initiated by regular cloud
        customers. It is mainly used by Bigquery to differentiate between
        requests coming from regular cloud customers and internal Google
        systems. Please refer to go/bq-dma-new-processing-purpose for more
        details.
      ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT: Data is being processed to handle a user request to
        manage their account.
      USER_COMMUNICATIONS: Data is being processed to send communications to
        users.
      MODEL_TRAINING: Model training as a processing purpose was introduced
        for complying with the Search Model training Privacy Control (SMPC)
        policy: go/smpc-program, go/ptoken-dga-smpc. While this purpose
        doesn't really represent an end-goal, it was approved by legal and reg
        affairs and its naming aligns with external conversations and
        regulatory interest. For questions about this purpose contact pCounsel
        who/sjz.
      VERIFICATION_TESTING_VALIDATION: Processing for debugging or monitoring
        or somehow related to pure software functionality. Access in order to
        perform testing, verification, certification, or other routine or pre-
        launch analysis by using stored user data. This can include regression
        testing, load testing, unit/integration testing, or other analysis of
        machine-generated or replayed activity. This is done primarily for
        routinized, transient evaluation like testing new builds/deployments.
      DEBUGGING_AND_MONITORING: Processing for debugging or monitoring or
        somehow related to pure software functionality - analyzing user data
        to develop approved features, refactor or improve existing ones, or
        verify, triage, analyze, troubleshoot, or resolve problems with
        products and services
      INFRASTRUCTURE_METRICS: Any processing for the purpose of understanding
        how services / products are used by users, including traffic shaping,
        monitoring etc. Any processing necessary to monitor a service and its
        performance to maintain product excellence, reliability, service
        quality, or other technical measures as perceived by a user.
      DATA_RECOVERY: The data is being processed to detect, prevent, recover
        for data loss or corruption (in line with the purpose limitations
        documented at go/backups-user-data). See also go/dg-classification-
        backup-data.
      BUSINESS_ANALYSIS: Perform analysis to set strategy, prioritize
        features, assess business risks or otherwise use the data to derive
        insights for the benefits of the company or its product or service
        offering.
      MARKET_RESEARCH: This is for any analysis that looks at the existing
        market across companies / manufacturers, or generates leads, contacts
        or potential clients or users. This can be either for manual outreach,
        automatic outreach or internal use.
      RESEARCH_EXPERIMENTATION: Open-ended or undirected analysis of user data
        with a clear hypothesis or intended benefit in mind.
      TRUST_SAFETY: The data is being processed to protect Google, its users,
        customers or other stakeholders. This includes manual detection,
        analysis, remediation, prevention of unacceptable abusive behavior as
        defined by the terms of service. It also includes actions such as
        processing to keep accounts safe (such as processing for the purposes
        of auth or authz)
      TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_FRAUD: More specific Trust and safety purposes.
      TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_SPAM: <no description>
      TRUST_SAFETY_SECURITY: <no description>
      TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_ABUSE: <no description>
      COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT: Processing the data for compliance purposes,
        legal purpose, law enforcement requests and incident management
        related to any of these.
      LIMITED_MANUAL_ACCESS: <no description>
      COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT: <no description>
      COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT_LEGAL: <no description>
      COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT_CONSUMER: <no description>
      COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_ELI: <no description>
      EXP_MODEL_TRAINING_FOR_PRODUCTION: <no description>
      MODEL_GROUNDING: <no description>
    """
    PROCESSING_PURPOSE_UNSPECIFIED = 0
    PROCESSING_PURPOSE_NOTHING = 1
    PROVISION_OF_SERVICE = 2
    PROVISION_OF_SERVICE_INFRASTRUCTURE = 3
    ADS_RELATED_PROVISION_OF_SERVICE = 4
    PRODUCT_PERSONALIZATION = 5
    CONTEXTUALIZATION = 6
    REVENUE_GENERATION = 7
    USER_SUPPORT = 8
    CLOUD_PROCESSING_INFRASTRUCTURE = 9
    CLOUD_PROCESSING_INFRASTRUCTURE_VALIDATION = 10
    ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT = 11
    USER_COMMUNICATIONS = 12
    MODEL_TRAINING = 13
    VERIFICATION_TESTING_VALIDATION = 14
    DEBUGGING_AND_MONITORING = 15
    INFRASTRUCTURE_METRICS = 16
    DATA_RECOVERY = 17
    BUSINESS_ANALYSIS = 18
    MARKET_RESEARCH = 19
    RESEARCH_EXPERIMENTATION = 20
    TRUST_SAFETY = 21
    TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_FRAUD = 22
    TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_SPAM = 23
    TRUST_SAFETY_SECURITY = 24
    TRUST_SAFETY_ANTI_ABUSE = 25
    COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT = 26
    LIMITED_MANUAL_ACCESS = 27
    COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT = 28
    COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT_LEGAL = 29
    COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_TAKEOUT_CONSUMER = 30
    COMPLIANCE_LEGAL_SUPPORT_ELI = 31
    EXP_MODEL_TRAINING_FOR_PRODUCTION = 32
    MODEL_GROUNDING = 33

